oopener noreferrer">Amended Complaint</a> </p><p>2025-04-29</p></td><td cla=
ss=3D"column-3">2025-03-11</td><td class=3D"column-4">Plaintiff-side&nbsp;S=
tate&nbsp;Amicus</td><td class=3D"column-5">Government Action Blocked</td><=
td class=3D"column-8">2026-04-03</td><td class=3D"column-9 none dtr-hidden"=
 style=3D"display: none;"><p>On March 6, 2025, President Donald Trump issue=
d an executive order (EO) accusing the law firm Perkins Coie LLP of undermi=
ning democracy and maintaining illegal race-based hiring quotas. The execut=
ive order directs various agencies to impose sanctions against the firm, in=
cluding: terminating the firm=E2=80=99s government contracts; suspending em=
ployees=E2=80=99 security clearances pending a national-security review; or=
dering a review of the firm=E2=80=99s hiring practices by the Equal Employm=
ent Opportunity Commission; limiting employees=E2=80=99 access to federal b=
uildings; and directing agencies not to hire Perkins Coie employees. Plaint=
iff <a href=3D"https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.278=
290/gov.uscourts.dcd.278290.1.0_1.pdf" aria-label=3D"sued- opens in new tab=
" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">sued</a> on March 11, alleg=
ing that the executive action is unconstitutional, violating separation of =
powers, the First Amendment=E2=80=99s protections for freedom of speech and=
 association, the Fifth Amendment=E2=80=99s Due Process Clause, the Fifth a=
nd Sixth Amendment=E2=80=99s right to counsel, and the Fourteenth Amendment=
=E2=80=99s Equal Protection Clause. They seek a declaratory judgment that t=
he order is unconstitutional and an immediate injunction stopping implement=
ation of the order pending court review, followed by preliminary and perman=
ent injunctions. The Plaintiff also submitted a request for a temporary res=
training order and a proposed order that enjoined only Sections 1 (Purpose)=
, 3 (Contracting), and 5 (Personnel including access to Federal Government =
buildings) of the executive order.</p></td><td class=3D"column-10 none dtr-=
hidden" style=3D"display: none;"><p><strong><strong>March 12, 2025:</strong=
></strong> State Attorneys General submitted an <a href=3D"https://storage.=
courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.278290/gov.uscourts.dcd.278290.15.=
0_5.pdf" aria-label=3D"amicus brief- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" re=
l=3D"noopener noreferrer">amicus brief</a> in support of Plaintiffs.</p><p>=
<strong><strong>March 12, 2025:</strong></strong> Judge Beryl Howell, <a hr=
ef=3D"https://news.bloomberglaw.com/product/blaw/bloomberglawnews/exp/eyJpZ=
CI6IjAwMDAwMTk1LThhZGUtZDk1NC1hZGQ1LWVmZmZhZTNmMDAwMSIsImN0eHQiOiJCVU5XIiwi=
dXVpZCI6IkY1YzdKQjUrRlpSVTBUenUrZ05sSEE9PWszQ2JVaWdOdXBQM1dhWXJpbXpDa2c9PSI=
