against Kristi Noem, the Secretary of the Department of Homeland Security (=
DHS), in her official capacity, alleging that, pursuant to the Executive Or=
der, TSA issued a directive prohibiting Plaintiff and all other transgender=
 TSOs from conducting security pat-downs of airline passengers and disallow=
ing their use of TSA-controlled restrooms that align with their gender iden=
tity. Plaintiff alleges this directive interferes with her ability to perfo=
rm her regularly assigned job duties, places undue burden on her female cow=
orkers, subjects her to unwanted stigma and disclosure of her gender identi=
ty, and will impede her career advancement. Plaintiff alleges the directive=
 violates Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 (Title VII), which prot=
ects Plaintiff from sex and gender identity discrimination. Plaintiff prima=
rily requests that the court declare that the actions of Defendant violate =
Title VII; enjoin Defendant from implementing or enforcing the Executive Or=
der and any other similar policy or practice; and award her compensatory da=
mages.</p></span></li><li class=3D" none" data-dtr-index=3D"9" data-dt-row=
