neral to enforce a new statutory interpretation to disallow counting of bal=
lots received after Election Day; and (6) Section 7(b), which directs the E=
AC to condition funding to States based on adherence to this interpretation=
 of Election Day. Plaintiffs allege that the President does not have author=
ity to implement these changes to election law. Specifically, they argue th=
at these provisions of the EO are unconstitutional under the Bicameralism, =
Presentment, Elections, and Electors Clauses (depending on the provisions),=
