s; (5) Section 7(a), which directs the Attorney General to enforce a new st=
atutory interpretation to disallow counting of ballots received after Elect=
ion Day; and (6) Section 7(b), which directs the EAC to condition funding t=
o States based on adherence to this interpretation of Election Day. Plainti=
ffs allege that the President does not have authority to implement these ch=
anges to election law. Specifically, they argue that these provisions of th=
e EO are unconstitutional under the Bicameralism, Presentment, Elections, a=
nd Electors Clauses (depending on the provisions), ultra vires, in violatio=
n of the National Voter Registration Act, violate Separation of Powers, and=
 violate State sovereignty. Plaintiffs have requested the court declare the=
 challenged provisions unconstitutional and void, and to preliminarily and =
permanently enjoin all Defendants except Trump from implementing or enforci=
ng the challenged provisions.</p></span></li><li class=3D" none" data-dtr-i=
