 Court held that although the CSRA=E2=80=99s administrative scheme would no=
rmally be the appropriate venue for this case, the CSRA =E2=80=9Crequires a=
 strong and independent Merit Systems Protections Board (MSPB) and Special =
Counsel=E2=80=9D and stated that the principle that =E2=80=9Cfunctioning an=
d independent bodies would receive, review, and decide in the first instanc=
e challenges to adverse personnel actions affecting covered federal employe=
es has recently been called into question.=E2=80=9D In particular, the pane=
l noted that =E2=80=9Cthe Special Counsel and several members of the MSPB h=
ave been terminated by the President and the Government has questioned the =
constitutionality of the removal protections enshrined in the CSRA.=E2=80=
=9D</p><p>The Court vacated the case and remanded so that the District Cour=
t can evaluate whether the CSRA continues to function as Congress intended =
in order to determine whether it would be appropriate to strip jurisdiction=
