=99s ability to draw down funds previously obligated to SEF and issued a Gr=
ant Award Notification (GAN) terminating SEF=E2=80=99s grant and project. T=
he Termination Letter asserted that the funding that supported the EAC-Sout=
h promoted initiatives that were discriminatory and violated federal civil =
rights laws. SEF contends that since the termination, it has not received p=
ending payments owed to it and that will result in the permanent closure of=
 SEF, thus causing significant harm to both it and to the constituents it s=
erves.</p><p>The Plaintiff sued, asserting that the termination violates th=
e Administrative Procedure Act (APA) as arbitrary and capricious, contrary =
