ent Trump, rather than the contest-winning image of a national park. Plaint=
iffs allege this action disregards the public participation requirements of=
 the statute, and betrays the expectations of the thousands of people who p=
articipate in the contest. Plaintiffs seek declaratory relief, and ask the =
court to remand Defendants=E2=80=99 decisions related to the 2026 national =
park passes, and enjoin Defendants=E2=80=99 use of any pass that unlawfully=
