es of firearms, including weapons defined as =E2=80=9Ca machinegun=E2=80=9D=
. Machinegun conversion devices (MCDs) are devices that are used to convert=
 a semi-automatic firearm, which requires a shooter to release and pull the=
 trigger for each shot they fire, into a machinegun that fires automaticall=
y. The =E2=80=9Cforced reset trigger,=E2=80=9D or =E2=80=9CFRT,=E2=80=9D is=
 a type of MCD that is designed to replace the standard trigger assembly on=
 an AR-15-type rifle. Since the 1970s, the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Fire=
arms, and Explosives (ATF) has consistently classified devices functionally=
 similar to FRTs as prohibited machineguns under federal law.</p><p>Over th=
e last few years, ATF undertook enforcement efforts that succeeded in enjoi=
ning distributors from selling FRTs and FRT equipped weapons, and conducted=
 extensive retrieval operations, seizing nearly 12,000 FRTs from the field.=
 In 2023, ATF brought an enforcement action against Defendant Rare Breed Tr=
iggers (RBG) in New York, after which the district court issued a prelimina=
ry injunction against the continued distribution of FRT=E2=80=99s (subseque=
ntly appealed to the Second Circuit), and a civil forfeiture action in the =
District of Utah against certain of RBG=E2=80=99s subcontractors (collectiv=
ely, the RBG Defendants).</p><p>In August 2023, Defendant National Associat=
ion of Gun rights (NAGR) challenged the ATF=E2=80=99s classifications of th=
e FRT-15 as machineguns in the Northern District of Texas, and in July 2024=
, the district court granted plaintiffs=E2=80=99 motion for summary judgmen=
t and vacated and set aside the challenged classifications, enjoined the Un=
ited States from implementing or enforcing ATF=E2=80=99s =E2=80=9Cexpanded =
definition of =E2=80=98machinegun=E2=80=99=E2=80=9D against the plaintiffs =
to the suit, enjoined the United States from pursuing criminal enforcement =
actions against the RBT Defendants, and ordered the United States to return=
 any FRTs =E2=80=9Cseized pursuant to their unlawful classification=E2=80=
=9D to all parties in that litigation within 30 days. The United States app=
ealed the NAGR decision.</p><p>On February 7, 2025, President Trump issued =
<a href=3D"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/02/protecti=
ng-second-amendment-rights/" aria-label=3D"Executive Order (EO) 14,206- ope=
ns in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">Executive Orde=
