y directives implementing the executive orders at the National Institutes o=
f Health (NIH). On April 4, 2025 the Commonwealth of Massachusetts and the =
attorneys general of 15 additional states sued the NIH and various institut=
es and centers administered by the NIH, as well as NIH director Dr. Jay Bha=
ttacharya, the Department of Health and Human Service (HHS), and HHS Secret=
ary Robert F. Kennedy Jr., for failure to properly review or administer NIH=
 grants and grant renewals. Plaintiffs allege that since January, all upcom=
ing meetings for NIH grant applications by the two NIH bodies who review gr=
ants (a group of subject matter experts and an advisory council that consid=
