D, HHS, and other agencies and government officials to challenge the new co=
nditions, arguing that they are being forced to make an impossible choice o=
f either fundamentally changing their programming and exposing themselves t=
o civil and criminal liability under the False Claims Act or ending their f=
ederally funding programs, which would have devastating impacts on those th=
ey serve. Plaintiffs argue that the government violated the separation of p=
owers, spending clause, First Amendment, and the Fifth Amendment=E2=80=99s =
Due Process Clause. They also argue that defendants violated the Administra=
tive Procedure Act for acting in excess of statutory authority, contrary to=
