on salmon hatchery funding pool established under the Inflation Reduction A=
ct. The administration's conduct involved NOAA leadership pre-selecting a "=
fixed" list of only 27 eligible tribes=E2=80=94providing each with $2 milli=
on non-competitive grants while excluding Plaintiffs=E2=80=94without provid=
ing a reasoned decision or public notice. These actions result in severe ha=
rms, as the lack of funding prevents the Colville Tribes from constructing =
a $13.2 million "third water source" necessary to mitigate rising temperatu=
res that cause high broodstock mortality, and denies the Chehalis Tribe $8.=
5 million for critical renovations to replace failing water towers and insu=
fficient wells. The Colville Tribes assert that its off-reservation fishing=
 rights are substantively identical to those of "treaty tribes" included on=
 the list, and its operations are comparable to the Metlakatla Indian Commu=
nity, which was deemed eligible. The Chehalis Tribe argues its on-reservati=
on fishing rights and hatchery operations are comparable to the Hoopa and Y=
urok Tribes, both of which were included. Furthermore, Plaintiffs allege th=
at NOAA failed to provide consistent notice of tribal consultation sessions=
, further marginalizing their ability to advocate for inclusion. The compla=
int alleges that Defendants=E2=80=99 exclusion of the Colville and Chehalis=
 Tribes is in violation of the Indian Reorganization Act=E2=80=99s "Privile=
ges and Immunities" clause, 25 U.S.C. =C2=A7 5123(f), the Administrative Pr=
ocedure Act (APA), 5 U.S.C. =C2=A7 706, for arbitrary and capricious action=
s and the unlawful withholding of a reasoned decision, and a breach of the =
federal government=E2=80=99s fiduciary trust responsibilities. To remedy th=
ese violations, Plaintiffs seek a declaratory judgment of their eligibility=
, an order for the immediate distribution of $2 million grants to each Trib=
e, and a requirement that Defendants preserve $18 million in remaining fund=
s until their project proposals are evaluated.</p></td><td class=3D"column-=
