ve information. Plaintiffs further argue that the Challenged Surveillance P=
rogram is arbitrary and capricious agency action, exceeds authority, and is=
 contrary to the law in violation of the Administrative Procedure Act. They=
 seek declaratory and injunctive relief barring the government from continu=
ing the surveillance and retaliatory enforcement.</p></td><td class=3D"colu=
