tay</a> in the case until 12 pm on Feb. 24 to allow the government time to =
gather information to respond, and time for expedited briefing. The court f=
urther ordered the Defendants to respond to Plaintiffs=E2=80=99 Feb. 19 eme=
rgency motion for a stay of removal by Feb. 21.</p><p><strong><strong>Feb. =
22, 2025:</strong></strong> Judge Moss <a href=3D"https://storage.courtlist=
ener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.277039/gov.uscourts.dcd.277039.23.0.pdf" ar=
ia-label=3D"denied- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener nor=
eferrer">denied</a> as moot the emergency motion to stay removal of individ=
ual Plaintiffs because the government agreed not to use Proclamation 10888 =
to remove them during the litigation. The court ordered that the government=
 must provide at least seven days=E2=80=99 notice before removing any indiv=
idual Plaintiffs during the case and vacated the scheduled hearing.</p><p><=
strong><strong>Feb. 26, 2025:</strong></strong> At the parties=E2=80=99 req=
uest, the court <a href=3D"https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/69606027/re=
fugee-and-immigrant-center-for-education-and-legal-services-v-noem/#minute-=
entry-417620829" aria-label=3D"agreed- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" =
rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">agreed</a> to treat Plaintiffs=E2=80=99 Feb. 19=
 motion for a classwide preliminary injunction as a motion for summary judg=
ment.</p><p><strong><strong>March 24, 2025:</strong></strong> The Trump adm=
inistration <a href=3D"https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts=
.dcd.277039/gov.uscourts.dcd.277039.44.0.pdf" aria-label=3D"filed- opens in=
 new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">filed</a> a motion =
for summary judgment, asserting, among other things, that plaintiffs lack s=
tanding, that presidential decisions are not reviewable under the APA, and =
that the =E2=80=9C[t]he determination that the United States is facing an i=
nvasion is an unreviewable political question.=E2=80=9D</p><p><strong><stro=
