<td class=3D"column-3">2026-01-28</td><td class=3D"column-4">Plaintiff-side=
&nbsp;State&nbsp;Amicus</td><td class=3D"column-5">Government Action Tempor=
arily Blocked</td><td class=3D"column-8">2026-02-27</td><td class=3D"column=
-9 none dtr-hidden" style=3D"display: none;"><p>In early January 2026, the =
Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and U.S. Citizenship and Immigration =
Services (USCIS) launched Operation Post-Admission Refugee Reverification a=
nd Integrity Strengthening (=E2=80=9C<a href=3D"https://www.uscis.gov/newsr=
oom/news-releases/dhs-launches-landmark-uscis-fraud-investigation-in-minnes=
ota" aria-label=3D"Operation PARRIS- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" re=
l=3D"noopener noreferrer">Operation PARRIS</a>=E2=80=9D) which had the stat=
ed purpose of targeting and re-examining the legal status of Minnesota=E2=
=80=99s 5,600 refugees who have not yet secured permanent resident status (=
green cards). The individuals targeted are lawful refugees who were admitte=
d to the country, have followed the rules, and are waiting to have their st=
atus adjusted to lawful permanent residents, which is possible after being =
present in the US for at least one year. On Jan. 18, 2026, Plaintiff U.H.A.=
 <a href=3D"https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/72157874/uha-v-bondi/#entr=
y-1" aria-label=3D"filed- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopen=
er noreferrer">filed</a> a Petition for Writ of Habeas Corpus following his=
 arrest and detention under Operation PARRISS and on the same day the court=
 <a href=3D"https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/72157874/uha-v-bondi/#entr=
y-3" aria-label=3D"enjoined- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noo=
pener noreferrer">enjoined</a> the government from removing, transferring, =
or otherwise facilitating the removal of Petitioner from the District of Mi=
nnesota. On Jan. 24 a group of refugees living in Minnesota, along with a l=
egal services nonprofit, joined U.H.A. to file <a href=3D"https://www.thead=
vocatesforhumanrights.org/Res/UHA-v-Bondi-Filed-Complaint-and-Amended-Petit=
ion.pdf" aria-label=3D"a class action complaint- opens in new tab" target=
=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">a class action complaint</a> agains=
t DHS seeking to end Operation Parris and the policies under which it has b=
een implemented, which they allege have included the forcible arrest of una=
djusted refugees without warrants or probable cause that they are removable=
 or a flight risk; unauthorized detention, including in facilities outside =
the state; and coercive interrogation of refugees about their initial refug=
ee applications (=E2=80=9Cthe Refugee Detention Policy=E2=80=9D).</p><p>The=
 complaint asserts that internal DHS procedures make clear that a refugee=
=E2=80=99s failure to adjust status or to apply for adjustment of status is=
 not a ground for removal and therefore cannot be grounds for detention, an=
d that DHS regulations authorize arrest only when an immigration officer ha=
s reason to believe that a person has committed an offense or is illegally =
in the U.S., and requires that officers obtain a warrant unless the officer=
 believes the person will escape. Plaintiffs allege that the Refugee Detent=
ion Policy violates the Accardi Doctrine, which requires that agencies foll=
ow their own procedures, the Administrative Procedure Act as contrary to la=
w, arbitrary and capricious and in disregard of statutorily required proced=
ures, the Fourth Amendment=E2=80=99s prohibition on warrantless seizure, an=
d the Fifth Amendment=E2=80=99s guarantees of Due Process and Equal Protect=
ion. They seek to certify a class of =E2=80=9C[a]ll individuals with refuge=
e status who are residing in the state of Minnesota who have not yet adjust=
ed to lawful permanent resident status and have not been charged with any g=
round for removal under the [Immigration and Nationality Act]=E2=80=9D (the=
 Class) and a =E2=80=9Cdetained subclass=E2=80=9D defined as =E2=80=9C[a]ll=
 members of the Class who are or will be detained by DHS pursuant to the Re=
fugee Detention Policy=E2=80=9D (the Detained Subclass), a declaration that=
 the Refugee Detention Policy is unlawful and unconstitutional, and to vaca=
te and postpone the effective date of the Refugee Detention Policy. On the =
same day, plaintiffs filed a <a href=3D"https://www.courtlistener.com/docke=
t/72157874/uha-v-bondi/" aria-label=3D"separate motion to certify the Class=
 and Detained Subclass- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener=
 noreferrer">separate motion to certify the Class and Detained Subclass</a>=
 and a <a href=3D"https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/72157874/uha-v-bondi=
/" aria-label=3D"motion for a temporary restraining order- opens in new tab=
" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">motion for a temporary rest=
raining order</a> seeking to enjoin the arrest or detention of any unadjust=
ed refugee and an order that any member of the Class currently in detention=
 be released.</p></td><td class=3D"column-10 none dtr-hidden" style=3D"disp=
lay: none;"><p><strong><strong>Jan. 18, 2026:</strong></strong> The court <=
a href=3D"https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/72157874/uha-v-bondi/#entry-=
3" aria-label=3D"enjoined- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noope=
ner noreferrer">enjoined</a> the government from removing, transferring, or=
 otherwise facilitating the removal of Petitioner from the District of Minn=
