it- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">suit</a=
> challenging her dismissal by President Trump. Describing her removal as =
=E2=80=9Cunprecedented and illegal,=E2=80=9D Cook alleges that under the Fe=
deral Reserve Act she can only be removed for =E2=80=9Cjust cause,=E2=80=9D=
 which President Trump has failed to demonstrate. She further argues that h=
er termination violates the Due Process Clause of the Fifth Amendment. She =
is seeking a declaratory judgment that her firing is unlawful as well as an=
 injunction against the Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System fr=
om removing her from office.</p></td><td class=3D"column-10 none dtr-hidden=
" style=3D"display: none;"><p><strong><strong>Aug. 29, 2025:</strong></stro=
ng> President Trump <a href=3D"https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.=
uscourts.dcd.284270/gov.uscourts.dcd.284270.13.0_1.pdf" aria-label=3D"oppos=
ed- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">opposed=
</a> Cook=E2=80=99s motion for a temporary restraining order, arguing the F=
ederal Reserve Act gives the President broad discretion to remove a Governo=
r =E2=80=9Cfor cause,=E2=80=9D and that Cook=E2=80=99s alleged false mortga=
ge statements meet that standard. The Board of Governors of the Federal Res=
erve System and Chairman Jerome Powell separately filed a <a href=3D"https:=
//storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.284270/gov.uscourts.dcd.=
284270.12.0_5.pdf" aria-label=3D"response- opens in new tab" target=3D"_bla=
nk" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">response</a> to Cook=E2=80=99s motion, stat=
ing they were named in the suit only to ensure complete relief if Cook prev=
ails and do not plan to argue the TRO motion. They expressed interest in a =
prompt ruling to remove uncertainty and confirmed they will comply with any=
 court order.</p><p><strong>Sept. 9, 2025:</strong> In place of a TRO, Dist=
rict Court Judge Jia Cobb issued a <a href=3D"https://ecf.dcd.uscourts.gov/=
