r is likely unlawful. The court held that the cited mortgage fraud allegati=
on predated her appointment and therefore did not meet the =E2=80=9Cfor cau=
se=E2=80=9D removal standard. Judge Cobb also found that the administration=
 likely violated Cook=E2=80=99s due process rights by not giving her a mean=
ingful opportunity to be heard prior to her firing.</p><p><strong>Sept. 10,=
 2025:</strong> The Trump administration filed an <a href=3D"https://storag=
e.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.284270/gov.uscourts.dcd.284270.3=
0.0_3.pdf" aria-label=3D"appeal- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D=
"noopener noreferrer">appeal</a> of the <a href=3D"https://ecf.dcd.uscourts=
.gov/cgi-bin/show_public_doc?2025cv2903-27" aria-label=3D"preliminary injun=
ction- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">prel=
iminary injunction</a> issued by Judge Cobb that restored Governor Cook to =
her position. The administration has also filed a <a href=3D"https://storag=
e.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cadc.42372/gov.uscourts.cadc.42372.0=
1208774677.0.pdf" aria-label=3D"motion- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank"=
 rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">motion</a> for an administrative stay and a st=
ay pending appeal to the D.C. Circuit, attempting to prevent Cook from rema=
ining in her position while litigation proceeds.</p><p><strong>Sept. 15, 20=
25:</strong> In a 2-1 decision, the D.C. Circuit <a href=3D"https://storage=
.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.cadc.42372/gov.uscourts.cadc.42372.01=
208775757.0.pdf" aria-label=3D"denied- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" =
rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">denied</a> the administration=E2=80=99s emergen=
cy motion for an administrative stay and a stay pending appeal, keeping Gov=
ernor Cook in her position while litigation proceeds. The majority determin=
ed that Cook=E2=80=99s due process claim was =E2=80=9Cvery likely meritorio=
us=E2=80=9D because she was given no notice or opportunity to respond befor=
e removal. The order allowed for Cook to <a href=3D"https://www.nytimes.com=
/2025/09/16/business/federal-reserve-trump-cook-miran.html" aria-label=3D"a=
ttend- opens in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">atte=
nd</a> the Board=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://www.federalreserve.gov/moneta=
rypolicy/fomc.htm" aria-label=3D"Federal Open Market Committee- opens in ne=
w tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">Federal Open Market Co=
mmittee</a> meeting on Tuesday, Sept. 16 in her capacity as a Federal Reser=
ve Board Governor. Judge Katsas dissented, arguing that =E2=80=9Cpublic off=
