he Lincoln Memorial Reflecting Pool with a vivid blue coating in advance of=
 the nation=E2=80=99s 250th anniversary celebration on July 4, 2026. The Re=
flecting Pool is part of the National Mall Historic District and is listed =
in the National Register of Historic Places; the NPS has previously identif=
ied its dark grey, achromatic basin, which was deliberately designed to cre=
ate the pool=E2=80=99s reflective depth, as a =E2=80=9Ccharacter-defining f=
eature=E2=80=9D subject to consultation and review processes under the Nati=
onal Historic Preservation Act (NHPA). NPS <a href=3D"https://www.washingto=
ntimes.com/news/2026/may/9/trump-reportedly-awards-no-bid-contract-man-work=
ed-personal-pool/" aria-label=3D"reportedly- opens in new tab" target=3D"_b=
lank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">reportedly</a> awarded a $6.9 million no-=
bid contract for the resurfacing without following proper consultation and =
review processes under the NHPA and the National Environmental Policy Act.<=
/p><p>On May 11, 2026, the Cultural Landscape Foundation (TCLF), a nonprofi=
t dedicated to the stewardship of historic designed landscapes, and Charles=
 A. Birnbaum, TCLF=E2=80=99s founder and a former NPS official who authored=
