ies, filed a <a href=3D"https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourt=
s.dcd.292242/gov.uscourts.dcd.292242.1.0.pdf" aria-label=3D"complaint- open=
s in new tab" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">complaint</a> a=
lleging that Defendants violated the Administrative Procedure Act (APA). Th=
ey allege that the administration illegally proceeded without completing ma=
ndatory consultation and processes under the NHPA and without preparing an =
Environmental Impact Statement as required by the National Environmental Po=
licy Act (NEPA). Plaintiffs also allege that TCLF was denied the right to p=
articipate as a consulting party and that Birnbaum has suffered concrete ae=
sthetic injury. Plaintiffs seek a declaration that the resurfacing violates=
 the NHPA, NEPA, and the APA; vacatur of any authorizing agency decision; p=
reliminary and permanent injunctions and a temporary stay halting further a=
lteration; and restoration of the Reflecting Pool=E2=80=99s historic elemen=
